.TH ARIO 1 "November 2026" "Ario" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ario \- terminal download manager powered by aria2
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ario
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Ario manages HTTP, HTTPS, and BitTorrent downloads in a terminal interface.
It supports batch import of URLs and magnet links from the clipboard, local
torrent files, and automatic file categorization.
.PP
Organize downloads into queues, prioritize their order, and limit how many run
at once. Each queue has its own retry and download settings, which can be
overridden for individual downloads.
.PP
Queues can run on one-time, daily, or weekly schedules with automatic start and
stop times, including overnight windows. Queue event commands can run when all
downloads succeed or when a queue runs out of work or reaches its scheduled stop.
.PP
By default, it starts a local daemon and aria2 automatically.
Downloads and scheduled queues can continue after the interface closes.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print command-line help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the installed version and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-glyphs " MODE"
Choose the icon style:
.BR nerd ,
.BR unicode ,
or
.BR ascii .
Overrides the configured glyph mode.
Also accepts
.BR \-\-glyphs=MODE .
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B ?
Show keyboard shortcuts from the main screen.
.TP
.B v
Import URLs and magnet links from the clipboard.
.TP
.B a
Add a local torrent file.
.TP
.B q
Close the interface from the main screen.
By default, the daemon stays running while downloads are active or scheduled
queues are enabled.
.SH FILES
.B tui.toml
contains interface settings;
.B server.toml
contains daemon settings.
Both are created on first launch in
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ario ,
or
.I \(ti/.config/ario
if unset, on Linux.
On macOS, they are in
.IR "\(ti/Library/Application Support/ario" .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ario_daemon (1),
.BR aria2c (1)
